{% block introduction %}
	<p>
AIDCAT-AP (AI DCAT-AP) is an Application Profile that extends MLDCAT-AP to describe AI systems and AI agents, together with their roles, interfaces, skills, capabilities and the software they use.

</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block summary %}
<section id="abstract">
    <h2>Abstract</h2>
AIDCAT-AP aims to describe AI systems and AI agents so that they can be discovered and compared in catalogues. It builds on the machine learning models, datasets and infrastructure of MLDCAT-AP.

Concepts coming from the AI Act, the Cloud and AI Development Act (CADA) and from agent descriptions such as A2A, MCP and OASF have been included, and a reference to them has been added for each class or property where needed, including those references to existing data models.

</section>
{% endblock %}

